// v1.5.4 (TV-2026-003): shell syntax in a path is refused, not quoted.
//
// There is no bad code in this file - the vulnerability was in the OUTPUT PATH,
// so the suite drives it through a flags file. The case exists so the guard
// cannot be removed without a failure.
//
// The quoting helper wrapped paths in DOUBLE quotes, and `$(...)` and backticks
// expand inside double quotes - so quoting never made a path safe, only made it
// look safe. Confirmed through `-o` and through HOME, which reaches the same
// helper via the run directory.

df main() -> void {
    echo!("this should never build");
}
